{"name":"Gala Pink","hex":"#b04b63","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gala","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Celebratory; festive."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Pomp, show, or festivity.","A competition."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gala"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gala (apple)","blocks":[{"text":"Gala is an apple cultivar with a sweet, mild flavor, a crisp but not hard texture, and a striped or mottled orange or reddish appearance. Originating from New Zealand in the 1930s, similar to most named apples it is clonally propagated. Easy to grow, the Gala is one of the top commercial apple varieties today and one of the most popular in North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Gala_apples_on_cloth.jpg/330px-Gala_apples_on_cloth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gala_(apple)","wikidata":"Q494259"},{"title":"Gala (singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Gala Rizzatto, known mononymously as Gala, is an Italian pop singer and songwriter. Her debut album Come into My Life included the multiplatinum singles \"Freed from Desire\", \"Let a Boy Cry\" and \"Come into My Life\" which reached the Top 3 in music charts across Europe, South America, Russia and the Middle East. Gala has sold over six million records worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Gala_Portrait_by_Juan_Valentin.tif/lossless-page1-330px-Gala_Portrait_by_Juan_Valentin.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gala_(singer)","wikidata":"Q236237"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/US_Apple_Production_5-yr_Average_%282021-25%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/US_Apple_Production_5-yr_Average_%282021-25%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The Gala is the most produced apple variety in the United States during the first half of the 2020s.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUS_Apple_Production_5-yr_Average_(2021-25).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/S%C3%BCdtiroler_Apfel_g.g.A_Gala.jpg/500px-S%C3%BCdtiroler_Apfel_g.g.A_Gala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/S%C3%BCdtiroler_Apfel_g.g.A_Gala.jpg/500px-S%C3%BCdtiroler_Apfel_g.g.A_Gala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gala apple from South Tyrol, Italy, with protected-origin (PDO) sticker.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AS%C3%BCdtiroler_Apfel_g.g.A_Gala.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Royal_Gala_apples_-_whole_and_halved.jpg/500px-Royal_Gala_apples_-_whole_and_halved.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm